o<ensure_plug> sub
; Ensure the ATC spindle is holding tool 1 (the short dummy/plug tool)
; before a fixed drill is engaged — keeps dust out of the spindle and keeps
; it clear of the workpiece while a drill is doing the cutting. Called from
; m6_remap.ngc's drill branches, which track "what's logically in the
; spindle right now" in the global #<_atc_cur_tool> (not #<_tool_in_spindle>,
; which the remap framework only updates once M6 finishes — mid-remap we
; need our own live bookkeeping).
o<already> if #<_atc_cur_tool> NE 1
    o<ret> if [#<_atc_cur_tool> GE 1] AND [#<_atc_cur_tool> LE 20]
        o<return_tool> call [#<_atc_cur_tool>]
    o<ret> endif
    o<fetch_tool> call [1]
    #<_atc_cur_tool> = 1
o<already> endif
o<ensure_plug> endsub
